<title>FRANCE: Tunisia buys four lots of barley at $136.72.</title>
<headline>Tunisia buys four lots of barley at $136.72.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia on Friday bought 100,000 tonnes of new crop, optional-origin barley in four cargoes of 25,000 tonnes each at a delivered price of $136.72 per tonne for each cargo, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>Shipment dates are September 5-15, October 1-10, October 20-30 and November 20-30.</p>
<p>The deal is believed to be the first major grain contract made up entirely of new crop 1997/98 barley, the traders said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
